\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Energy spectrum of $^{87}\text {Sr}$ including fine and hyperfine interactions. In blue the $461~$nm transition used for TC, Zeeman cooling, blue MOT stage and imaging. The purple arrow indicates the repump line at $403~$nm from the metastable state $^3P_2$ used for the atoms leaking from the $^1P_1$ state. In red the transition at $689~$nm used for all stages of the red MOT, optical pumping, spin manipulation, coherent manipulation (see Chap.\ref {chap 2}), photoassociation (see Chap.\ref {chap 3})}}{5}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces Experimental sequence for the magnetic field, lasers intensity and frequencies depending on the time. In the bottom right corner is the detailed imaging sequence. }}{6}{figure.caption.10}%
